remembering a life taken too soon avid  motorcycle rider william defalco was  killed in a crash last saturday in north  las vegas tonight his friends and family  are coming together near the crash site  to honor him madison kimbrough joins us  live near craig and decatur with a look  ahead of that ceremony madison  we're here at craig road car wash where  defalco was a manager for almost two  decades and everyone here will  participate in the vigil happening  tonight near anne road at 6 p.m now to  give you a bit of a backstory defalco  was riding his motorcycle to work last  saturday morning when he was hit by a  speeding sedan that ran a red light that  sedan crashed into his motorcycle on ann  road and defalco was declared dead on  scene tonight we hear from his family  and friends remembering the cuban native  who built a community here in las vegas  around craig road car wash and detail  center fellow co-worker charlie drake  used to ride with defalco and says ever  since the crash he's been lost  i haven't touched my motorcycle since  last week i parked it  i don't know what to do yet it's just  not going to be the same for us here  i lost a brother co-worker and a friend  as for the man who hit him 29-year-old  thomas munoz was arrested and faces  several charges including dui causing  death again the vigil starts at 6 p.m  near the crash site 8 news now has been  invited to the vigil so we will be  bringing you live coverage reporting  near craig and decatur madison kimbrough  live local now
 

